---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT, REPO } from "../links";
---
<Base title="Terms of sale" description="What you buy with a whereti supporter license, how it is delivered, and how refunds work." prose>
  <h1>Terms of sale</h1>
  <p class="lead">For the whereti supporter license. The app itself is free and needs none of this.</p>

  <h2>What you buy</h2>
  <p>
    A supporter license is a digital product: a license key for whereti, issued in your name or your company's name,
    for a one-time payment.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Personal, $19:</strong> one person, on all their PCs.</li>
    <li><strong>Business, $39 per PC:</strong> a company, for as many PCs as it buys, with an invoice in the company's name.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Entered in whereti (Settings, Support), the key registers your copy to that name, which whereti then shows. It is
    valid for life, for this and every future version, and works offline. It is not a subscription and never renews.
  </p>

  <h2>Who sells it</h2>
  <p>
    The license is sold through Lemon Squeezy, the merchant of record: it takes the payment, charges the VAT or sales
    tax due in your country, and issues the receipt and invoice. Its own terms cover the payment. whereti is made by
    SOFTWARE HIVE S.R.L., Romania (details in the <a href="/legal/">legal notice</a>).
  </p>

  <h2>Price</h2>
  <p>
    Prices are in US dollars. The checkout shows the final price, with any tax, before you pay.
  </p>

  <h2>Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    The key is e-mailed within minutes of the payment, from licenses@whereti.com. If it has not arrived within an
    hour, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> with your order number.
  </p>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Within 14 days of the purchase you can have your money back, without giving a reason: write to
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> with your order number. The refund goes back the way you paid, through
    Lemon Squeezy.
  </p>

  <h2>The software</h2>
  <p>
    whereti is free software under the <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT license</a>, provided as it is. The
    supporter license does not change those terms, and nothing in whereti stops working without it.
  </p>

  <h2>Law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms follow Romanian law. If you buy as a consumer, you keep every right the law of your own country gives
    you. Write to us first at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>; in Romania, the consumer protection
    authority is <a href="https://anpc.ro">ANPC</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
